      "text": "All eight deliverables are written and mutually consistent (verified: allocations sum to £37,500 within the £48,000 envelope; metric names, pilot name, and uncertainty IDs match across `decisions.json` and the Markdown).\n\nThe chosen pilot is the **Evening Access Pilot** — thirteen Thursday openings coupled with the Northside–Kiln Field late minibus, at **£24,000** (£9,600 evening opening + £14,400 bus subsidy), sitting inside a **£37,500** committed plan with the rest of the envelope left unspent and lapsing. It is chosen because the 2023 pilot is the only quasi-experiment in the pack — +38% evening attendance with the minibus, back to baseline within six weeks of it stopping — which isolates transport rather than programme or awareness as the binding constraint, and because the budget reflects that opening and transport are worthless and actively misleading when funded alone. I deliberately excluded the £22,000 lift repair (capital, six-week lead, no costed first-floor programme, and unaffordable alongside the evidenced core), the £9,000 borough print campaign (tested and failed in 2022, and forbidden by board minute), and the £7,500 café refresh (unrelated to programming), and I left £10,500 uncommitted rather than fill the number with spend the evidence does not support.",
